id: pm-csv-mua3
title: A truncated list-all answer is consumed as if it were complete
description: "All three list-all call sites (loadKeyIndex for upsert key matching, loadAppliedByTransaction for atomic-import resume scans, buildCsvExport for CSV export) read .items from the pm list-all --json envelope without checking the envelope's completeness receipt. Verified on this host against the 682-item workspace: pm 2026.8.14 returned 10 items with truncated=true, so a CSV export silently shipped 10 of 682 rows reporting success, a resume scan silently saw none of the applied rows (re-importing on resume), and an upsert key index silently missed keys (creating duplicates). 2026.8.15 fixes the default, but truncated can still go true under an output budget and completeness.status can go partial when items are unreadable — each must refuse loudly instead of producing a partial answer that reports success. Related: @unbrained/pm-cli resolves through floating ranges (^2026.8.6 dev, >=2026.8.3 peer), which is how the 2026.8.14 regression reached this package with no diff to review."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-15T11:07:00.769Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-20T19:53:49.377Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-15T11:31:09.602Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-15T11:31:09.602Z"
author: pi-agent
resolution: "All three list-all call sites now parse the full envelope and refuse an incomplete answer via assertListAllComplete, which trips on truncated, has_more, completeness.status other than complete, or omission_receipt.has_omissions, naming the tripped signal and the count-versus-total figures. No --limit is passed on any list-all read. The pm CLI is exact-pinned at 2026.8.15 in devDependencies with a >=2026.8.15 peer floor."
expected_result: "A truncated or degraded list-all envelope causes the command to fail loudly rather than producing a partial CSV export, a resume scan that re-imports applied rows, or an upsert key index that creates duplicates."
actual_result: "149 of 149 tests pass with the gate in place. Neutering assertListAllComplete to a no-op and rebuilding fails 7 tests, so the refusals are exercised rather than asserted vacuously. Verified against the real 2026.8.15 envelope on this host: count 682, total 682, truncated false, completeness.status complete."
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-15T12:28:44.885Z",pi-agent,"Review round two on PR 68. Four findings, all correct.\n\nCodeRabbit Critical, and the sharpest one: both readers caught a JSON parse failure and returned an empty collection, and the resume reader also returned an empty map on a nonzero pm exit. That is the same silent-partial failure the completeness gate exists to stop, sitting one line above it. The inconsistency was visible in the code: the comment at the resume reader literally says an incomplete envelope must refuse and NOT degrade to an empty map, directly below a catch block that degrades to an empty map. An empty key index makes upsert create duplicates; an empty resume map makes a resume re-import applied rows. Both now throw, naming the consequence.\n\nCodeRabbit Trivial, but a genuine hole: count and total were read only to decorate the other refusal messages. An envelope reporting count 10 of total 682 with every flag clear is internally inconsistent, and trusting the flags over the arithmetic would consume 10 rows as the whole workspace. The gate now refuses a self-contradictory receipt.\n\nCodeRabbit Trivial: nothing pinned the argv, so the no-limit contract was prose only. A well-meaning add-a-sensible-limit change would have passed review and broken large workspaces silently. The seam now records every argv and a test asserts no --limit reaches list-all; re-adding it fails that test.\n\nGreptile P2 and CodeRabbit Major: manifest.json declared pm_min_version 2026.7.28 while package.json peerDependencies said 2026.8.15. The same compatibility claim to two different installers, npm and the pm host, with nothing binding them. Manifest raised to 2026.8.15.\n\n151 of 151 tests pass, release:check exit 0."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-20T19:53:49.357Z",codex,"PR 73 CodeRabbit requested explicit null-status coverage for every whole-corpus consumer. The existing process/parse failure test now asserts ENOBUFS and ENOENT refusal for export,key-index,and transaction-resume readers; the focused test is green."
tests[1]{command,path,scope,timeout_seconds,pm_context_mode,note}:
  node --test --test-name-pattern='whole-tracker readers classify' test/list-all-completeness.test.ts,test/list-all-completeness.test.ts,project,60,tracker,null-status refusal across all readers
close_reason: "All three list-all call sites now parse the full envelope and refuse an incomplete answer via assertListAllComplete, which trips on truncated, has_more, completeness.status other than complete, or omission_receipt.has_omissions, naming the tripped signal and the count-versus-total figures. No --limit is passed on any list-all read. The pm CLI is exact-pinned at 2026.8.15 in devDependencies with a >=2026.8.15 peer floor."
